  "reason": "1) Evidence: RNA multiprofile with scvi_n200 + transformer aggregation is the clear best configuration so far (acc 0.653, F1 0.628), while both image-only models are very weak (resnet50: 0.208, ViT-L: 0.227). We have strong evidence that multiprofile scvi_n200 dominates, but zero evidence yet on whether adding the image modality via fusion improves on this RNA-only baseline. 2) This experiment tests whether concat-fusing the stronger image encoder (ViT-L) into the best RNA multiprofile configuration (scvi_n200, transformer aggregation) yields any gain over the 0.653 RNA-only baseline. It isolates the fusion question by holding the RNA side at its known-best setting and adding only the image branch. 3) Under a limited budget, this is the highest-value next step: the study's core question is whether multimodal profiling outperforms unimodal, and we should answer that before spending further experiments on other multimodal variants (different encoders, fusion types, or aggregations). If it fails to beat 0.653, it saves many downstream multimodal experiments; if it helps, it identifies a productive direction to refine."
